<title>USA: McDermott International cuts dividend.</title>
<headline>McDermott International cuts dividend.</headline>
<dateline>NEW ORLEANS 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>McDermott International Inc said on Thursday that it reduced its quarterly dividend to $0.05 a share from $0.25 a share because of its recent financial performance.</p>
<p>The company said on October 31 that a profitable fiscal 1997 was unlikely.</p>
<p>The reduction of the dividend should improve the company's cash flow and financial liquidity, McDermott said.</p>
<p>The dividend is payable January 1, 1997, to shareholders of record on December 16, 1996, the company said.</p>
